    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c24b2e2d60d629eb1b3a59199b803f4e9cd01957e24aeabd52c7a5d4dfe9e0fe",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source reuses exponential suppression of high-zero terms in two ways: prospectively, to translate a decimal target into a zero-height cutoff, and retrospectively, to predict how partial explicit sums should approach the generic value. When improvement departs from that regime and plateaus, the first inaccurate derivative can dominate the later suppressed terms and localize the numerical bottleneck.",
